Word-boundary data is generated from GraalVM CE 17.0.9+9.1 / OpenJDK 17.0.9,
using the ROOT word BreakIterator tables. The original Oracle and IBM notices
are preserved in StringLowerData.java and the complete upstream rules here.
The tables/rules and adapted WordBreaks.java retain GPLv2 with the Classpath
exception. The extraction tool is project-owned Apache 2.0.
WordBreaks preserves the ROOT boundary cursor algorithms (forward/backward
state transitions, following/isBoundary, UTF-16 cursor and cached boundary)
from the complete upstream RuleBasedBreakIterator source included here.

